A||||1||btoth||My CD Writer is being weird||||8||
Z||000000||btoth||10-28-2001||10:44 AM||||OK, the burner:  Yamaha 4x4x16 CD-R/RW.<BR>Using Adaptec Easy CD Creator 4 because it was all that would work with Win2k (my first problem with Win2k).  I used to just use the version that came with my burner when I had 98.  4 is a copy that I downloaded because it's just too expensive for what it is.  (I don't think that that's my problem though, it was a full CD image that I downloaded.)<P>I used to always use the Memorex 74min (before 80min was available).  I then noticed that all of a sudden whenever I recorded to one of the 74min CDRs that they wouldn't play in my car cd player (Sony brand).  I figured they must have changed what they were using to make the CDs.<P>Then the Memorex 80min came out.  These I had never had any problems with at all.  I stopped buying them recently because they seemed to be really easy to scratch and didn't last long before developing skips.<P>So I tried different brands:  Verbatim and Sony first.  Both of these worked great, except for one annoyance.  After I burn an audio CD, my CD Burner won't recognize them as an audio CD.  Normally no big deal, but I use that drive to rip MP3s from the CDs because my 33x CD-ROM sucks for ripping tracks off of CDs.  Why would it not recognize the CD <I>after</I> I record to it?<P>So here's the weird<I>er</I> part:  The other day I bought some Imations... because they were the last brand to try.  I burn some MP3s to the first CD.  After it was done I checked and yep, the burner actually <I>recognized</I> the CD!  But, it hasn't been able to recognize the last two that I burned (didn't changed any settings).<P>So I'm confused.  Apparently it's not consistent at all!  So is it the software? The media? Or is my burner just getting flaky???  This is annoying.<P>Thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-28-2001||08:36 PM||||do you get any errors?  buffer underruns etc?<BR>here is a few ideas, <P><BR>*try to burn at the slowest speed you can as a test..<P>*maybe try to do a test on it first..(test&record)<P>*try a scandisk/defrag<P>*anything new installed lately?<P>*end task everything but your explorer and systray before you burn<BR>*also try a fresh restart before you burn..<P>* try to burn from an image, bin,iso,etc<P><BR>also check out <A HREF="http://www.cdrom-prod.com/software.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cdrom-prod.com/software.html</A> <P><BR>take a look at CD-R Verifier v1.6.2 & CD-R Diagnostic v1.7.0<P>good luck!<P>||||reg||1
